WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:04.141
- Walk me through like this feud that you've
got with Dana White. Who started it?

00:00:04.908 --> 00:00:06.710
Who's gonna end it? How does it end?

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.546
I want, I want to know
what's going on with that.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.482
- It all started back in 2000.

00:00:14.751 --> 00:00:17.053
It started when I was fighting Ben Askren.

00:00:17.621 --> 00:00:23.860
And he said on a podcast,
on Mike Tyson's podcast,

00:00:24.161 --> 00:00:28.498
that he would bet a million dollars
that I would lose to Ben Askren.

00:00:28.965 --> 00:00:31.701
So that's where it all
started. And he then

00:00:32.836 --> 00:00:35.138
got Ben Askren to go and train

00:00:35.138 --> 00:00:38.074
with Freddie Roach,
who's like a legendary boxing trainer

00:00:38.742 --> 00:00:41.545
and was trying to, you know,
do all this stuff to get him to win.

00:00:41.812 --> 00:00:44.314
And we just started
going back and forth, and

00:00:45.816 --> 00:00:48.752
I beat Ben in a minute and 59 seconds.

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:51.922
And Dana was just silent.
He couldn't believe it.

00:00:51.955 --> 00:00:55.425
Of course, then his only thing is
so that he doesn't look like an idiot.

00:00:55.425 --> 00:00:59.463
It's to, you know, insinuate
that these are rigged. Insinuate that

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:00.964
these fights aren't real.

00:01:00.964 --> 00:01:04.801
He's doing anything to save his ass
because I'm beating all of the guys

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:09.139
that were dominant in his league, the UFC.

00:01:09.606 --> 00:01:13.109
And so it's a bad look for his whole
entire company and organization.

00:01:13.109 --> 00:01:14.911
So, you know, he's smart.

00:01:14.911 --> 00:01:17.180
He's a smart guy, super smart guy,

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.983
and he's going to do anything
he can to discredit me.

00:01:20.717 --> 00:01:23.453
But, again, it just
makes the numbers go up, and

00:01:25.622 --> 00:01:26.723
it is what it is.

00:01:26.723 --> 00:01:28.992
- Have you had any one on
one conversation with Dana?

00:01:29.693 --> 00:01:33.230
- I don't think so. No, I have not.

00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:36.366
- So all of this is just podcast, podcast.

00:01:36.433 --> 00:01:39.769
I say this, you say that.
Where's my money?
- Yeah.
- OK.

00:01:39.803 --> 00:01:41.037
- And now it's fun for me.

00:01:41.037 --> 00:01:43.240
- Yeah.
- Like, because I see how mad he gets.

00:01:43.607 --> 00:01:47.644
- And I'm just, like... That's what
people don't get. Like when I'm trolling,

00:01:48.245 --> 00:01:49.813
I'm having— I'm just laughing.

00:01:49.813 --> 00:01:54.217
Like, I'll just be sitting there
in my room on my phone just laughing

00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:58.855
at like all the jokes I'm making, and I see
how pissed off it makes these meatheads.

00:01:59.055 --> 00:02:02.192
I call them, like, meatheads
because they don't know anything

00:02:02.192 --> 00:02:06.296
or any other emotion than to just,
like, get angry and, like, react.

00:02:06.663 --> 00:02:08.765
So it's like they're my puppets,

00:02:08.765 --> 00:02:13.003
and I just get them to, like, react,
however exactly I want them to.

00:02:14.304 --> 00:02:15.906
And I'm just always one step ahead.

00:02:15.906 --> 00:02:17.007
So for me, it's just fun.

00:02:17.007 --> 00:02:19.943
Like, I see him get all mad
and say all this stuff.

00:02:19.943 --> 00:02:24.915
And, like, I just laugh at it
because he's an old, fat, miserable man,

00:02:25.949 --> 00:02:29.352
you know? So, it's just funny, man.

00:02:29.653 --> 00:02:31.555
- How does the feud end?

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.793
How do you want the feud to end?
- Man.

00:02:38.562 --> 00:02:41.598
I would say a sword battle to the death
would be pretty dope.

00:02:42.432 --> 00:02:45.769
- You versus Dana White.
- Pay per view.

00:02:46.903 --> 00:02:49.806
- Sword battle to the death.

00:02:49.806 --> 00:02:53.977
- No, I mean, who knows if it ends.
It might never end.

00:02:54.244 --> 00:02:59.282
- Mmhmm.
- I think eventually he's gonna
have to do business with me

00:02:59.616 --> 00:03:02.419
and let his UFC champions

00:03:02.686 --> 00:03:06.790
come over and box me. You know,
just like he did with Conor and Floyd.

00:03:06.823 --> 00:03:09.526
Cuz at the end of the day,
money talks, and

00:03:11.261 --> 00:03:13.597
he's a smart guy who wants
to make money for the UFC.

00:03:13.597 --> 00:03:17.434
So he's gonna let a champion come over
and we'll probably do a co-promotion

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:20.870
where I'm fighting Conor,
Kamaru Usman or whoever it is.

